# Lens
option.LENS_FLARE=Lens Flare
option.LENS_FLARE.comment=Master switch for the sun / moon flare (ghosts, starburst, halo, glare, dirt, streak)
option.LENS_FLARE_STRENGTH=Flare Strength
option.LENS_FLARE_STRENGTH.comment=Works with every lens. 1 = as designed (ghosts use physically computed reflectance)
option.LENS_PRESET=Lens
option.LENS_PRESET.comment=Picks the lens character (flare colors and shapes, starburst rays, aberrations). Individual strengths only apply with Custom (see Custom Lens). Toggles always apply. Sonnar to Fish-eye are computed from the patent prescriptions of real lenses: Sonnar = high contrast, few ghosts, slight pincushion. Summilux 35 = glow wide open, cat's eye bokeh, dark corners. Canon 50/1.2 = soft and low contrast wide open, background smears toward the edges, strong corner falloff. Hologon = straight lines across 110 degrees, strong corner falloff, fixed f/8 (FOV 68). Flektogon = wavy mustache distortion (FOV 54). Fish-eye = fisheye projection, straight lines bend (FOV 110, Fisheye Framing = Fit Width matches the real lens). Suggested FOV = the real lens's angle with the 36 mm width of the 35 mm frame fitted to the screen width (16:9 cuts the top and bottom of 3:2): vertical FOV = 2 atan(18 / f x 9 / 16). Gyogyotto = near-orthographic fisheye, edges squeezed harder than the Rokkor, fixed f/8. Ultra Wide-Heliar 12 = 121 degrees, plain barrel distortion, very dark corners even stopped down. New FD 14 = 114 degrees, barrel distortion that eases off at the corners, dark corners wide open that recover when stopped down. STF 135 = apodization filter, out-of-focus highlights melt away without a rim. FA 28 Soft = soft focus halo wide open that disappears by f/5.6 (set the aperture with Depth of Field). Canon 50/0.95 = the darkest corners, glow only wide open. 35 mm = 32, 20 mm = 54, 15 mm = 68. 50 mm and longer need less than the game's minimum of 30, so use 30 (still wider than the real lens)
